1
00:00:01,340 --> 00:00:03,297
Residents report problems.

2
00:00:03,297 --> 00:00:08,867
Property managers coordinate staff, contractors, approvals and follow-ups.

3
00:00:08,867 --> 00:00:13,007
Relay brings that process into one AI-powered workflow.

4
00:00:13,007 --> 00:00:18,050
This is the manager's command center: what needs a person, and why.

5
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:23,929
Priya, a resident, reports a leak from a phone, in plain words.

6
00:00:23,929 --> 00:00:25,458
This is the text chat.

7
00:00:25,458 --> 00:00:29,420
Voice intake uses the same path, but it isn't shown here.

8
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:34,842
Relay's replies come from a local language model, running as a background job.

9
00:00:34,842 --> 00:00:38,735
Its thinking time is cut from the recording, and marked.

10
00:00:38,735 --> 00:00:41,098
It asks what it needs, then files.

11
00:00:41,098 --> 00:00:47,910
The case is saved by the server, and the confirmation comes from the database, not from the model.

12
00:00:56,657 --> 00:01:02,764
Morgan, the property manager, sees Priya's new case at the top of the queue, and opens it.

13
00:01:02,764 --> 00:01:08,193
The case workspace shows what Priya reported, and what Relay understood from it,

14
00:01:08,193 --> 00:01:12,400
with its assumptions kept apart from what Priya actually said.

15
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:18,643
"What Relay did" lists the coordinator's real tool calls, and what policy did with each one.

16
00:01:18,643 --> 00:01:20,611
It also suggested escalating.

17
00:01:20,611 --> 00:01:27,329
The safety rules found no hazard in Priya's words, so that stays a suggestion for Morgan to decide.

18
00:01:27,329 --> 00:01:31,468
Relay proposed Harbour Plumbing & Drain, an approved plumber.

19
00:01:31,468 --> 00:01:37,847
Autopilot is off at this property, so the offer waits for Morgan, who reviews it and sends it.

20
00:01:42,347 --> 00:01:47,275
Separately, an air-conditioning report came in from the same building,

21
00:01:47,275 --> 00:01:50,937
where no heating and cooling contractor is approved.

22
00:01:50,937 --> 00:01:52,345
Relay spots the gap.

23
00:01:52,345 --> 00:01:58,048
At this building it asks before spending anything, so Morgan approves one search.

24
00:01:58,048 --> 00:02:00,301
This is a live call to Fiber AI.

25
00:02:00,301 --> 00:02:04,948
Twenty real local businesses came back, Relay kept the best three,

26
00:02:04,948 --> 00:02:10,017
and the provider's charge, two credits, is recorded exactly as returned.

27
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:11,848
Discovery is not approval.

28
00:02:11,848 --> 00:02:17,832
Nobody has checked a licence or insurance, and Relay never contacts these businesses.

29
00:02:17,832 --> 00:02:21,212
Morgan only shortlists one, to check personally.

30
00:02:25,712 --> 00:02:26,904
Back to the leak.

31
00:02:26,904 --> 00:02:33,076
Jo, from Harbour Plumbing & Drain, a fictional test contractor, gets the offer by phone.

32
00:02:33,076 --> 00:02:39,458
Jo reads the request, accepts the job with an estimate of three hundred and twenty dollars,

33
00:02:39,458 --> 00:02:41,492
and proposes two visit times.

34
00:02:45,992 --> 00:02:51,077
Three hundred and twenty dollars is over this building's approval threshold,

35
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:54,689
so the money decision goes to Morgan, never to the AI.

36
00:02:54,689 --> 00:02:59,105
Morgan approves it, with a cap of three hundred and fifty dollars.

37
00:02:59,105 --> 00:03:01,447
The next step now belongs to Priya.

38
00:03:06,173 --> 00:03:09,432
Priya sees the proposed times, and picks one.

39
00:03:09,432 --> 00:03:11,098
The visit is confirmed.

40
00:03:15,598 --> 00:03:19,548
Jo starts the work, and reports exactly what was done.

41
00:03:24,552 --> 00:03:27,889
But finished work isn't the same as a solved problem.

42
00:03:27,889 --> 00:03:31,352
Relay asks Priya whether it's really fixed, in the app,

43
00:03:35,852 --> 00:03:36,814
and by email.

44
00:03:36,814 --> 00:03:39,477
This is Mailpit, a local test inbox.

45
00:03:39,477 --> 00:03:44,952
Relay records this email as captured by a test server, never as delivered.

46
00:03:46,988 --> 00:03:50,763
Priya confirms it's fixed, and the case is resolved.

47
00:03:55,057 --> 00:03:57,868
A repair that doesn't hold is handled too.

48
00:03:57,868 --> 00:04:01,549
Daniel's dishwasher was repaired, but it stopped again.

49
00:04:01,549 --> 00:04:05,632
Daniel says so, and the case reopens for Morgan to follow up.

50
00:04:10,132 --> 00:04:16,207
When a request is unclear, Relay asks what is going on, instead of guessing a diagnosis.

51
00:04:20,707 --> 00:04:24,670
Possible emergencies and lockouts always go to a person.

52
00:04:24,670 --> 00:04:31,535
Water near a light fixture is escalated at once, and a lockout waits for staff to check identity.

53
00:04:31,535 --> 00:04:34,649
The safety rules are a net, not a guarantee.

54
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:39,744
In a held-out test, the system escalated eleven of thirteen emergencies,

55
00:04:39,744 --> 00:04:43,212
which is why anything uncertain goes to a person.

56
00:04:44,712 --> 00:04:50,537
And access is enforced by the server: Sam, from another firm, can't open this job.

57
00:04:55,037 --> 00:04:59,564
Back in Morgan's workspace: one report, one coordinated workflow,

58
00:04:59,564 --> 00:05:06,181
three people acting on the same case, every step recorded, a follow-up, and a verified outcome.

59
00:05:06,181 --> 00:05:10,290
The follow-up log shows each message's real delivery state.

60
00:05:10,290 --> 00:05:15,374
The local test mail server was briefly unreachable during this recording,

61
00:05:15,374 --> 00:05:18,717
so some emails are marked failed, not delivered.

62
00:05:20,217 --> 00:05:20,678
Relay.

63
00:05:20,678 --> 00:05:24,367
From resident request to accountable resolution.
